Date: Mon, 16 Feb 2026 09:44:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] CameraParameters: don't segfault on NULL key or value

Some vendor camera HALs pass NULL parameters to CameraParameters::set().
Without a guard, strchr() dereferences the null pointer and segfaults.
Add a NULL check for both key and value at the top of the method.

Change-Id: If48c430d76a585b72b691646e6972c1da228280c
---
 camera/CameraParameters.cpp | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/camera/CameraParameters.cpp b/camera/CameraParameters.cpp
index cd58d01..d64a659 100644
--- a/camera/CameraParameters.cpp
+++ b/camera/CameraParameters.cpp
@@ -238,6 +238,8 @@ void CameraParameters::unflatten(const String8 &params)

 void CameraParameters::set(const char *key, const char *value)
 {
+    if (key == NULL || value == NULL) return;
+
     // XXX i think i can do this with strspn()
     if (strchr(key, '=') || strchr(key, ';')) {
         //XXX ALOGE("Key \"%s\"contains invalid character (= or ;)", key);
